      "id": "ovBody",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -106.28714914415218,
      "y": 173.8531299901142,
      "width": 403.9655692121285,
      "height": 294.5582275505101,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2011,
      "versionNonce": 788633003,
      "boundElements": [],
      "text": "301core was a ground-up rewrite. The previous\nsystem had grown unmanageable, so we rebuilt the\ncore banking capabilities as a small set of clean,\nprovider-agnostic APIs — the building blocks every\nuser-facing product is assembled from.\n\nFour principles drove every decision: simplicity,\nobservability, ease of use and maintainability. We\nkept the surface small and the internals boring on\npurpose.\n\nEach API hides its vendors behind a single\ninterface. In production we ran two to three\ninterchangeable providers behind each API and could\nswap or add one without touching any caller.",
      "fontSize": 15.709772136027222,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "301core was a ground-up rewrite. The previous system had grown unmanageable, so we rebuilt the core banking capabilities as a small set of clean, provider-agnostic APIs — the building blocks every user-facing product is assembled from.\n\nFour principles drove every decision: simplicity, observability, ease of use and maintainability. We kept the surface small and the internals boring on purpose.\n\nEach API hides its vendors behind a single interface. In production we ran two to three interchangeable providers behind each API and could swap or add one without touching any caller.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "a0006",
      "autoResize": false
    },
